: "Conceptual modeling", "description": "This module builds directly on database purpose and architecture and develops conceptual modeling. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for relational model.", "children": [{"id": "615174ef-5aed-477c-9faa-557bdc6c586b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Entities", "children": [], "description": "Entities identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within conceptual modeling. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before relationships because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "d396f8e8-f5d2-4c6f-af94-5d198069994d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Relationships", "children": [], "description": "Relationships identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within conceptual modeling. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After entities, relationships supplies what is needed to address constraints."}, {"id": "45702a52-e593-4c95-b67e-491091329f42", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Constraints", "children": [], "description": "Constraints is a governing quantity in conceptual modeling, linking local calculations to system-level behavior and offering a consistency check. After relationships, constraints supplies what is needed to address er-to-relational mapping."}, {"id": "9e96863e-9e9b-4bab-89fd-190a1e3ca947", "type": "subtopic", "title": "ER-to-relational mapping", "children": [], "description": "ER-to-relational mapping gives conceptual modeling a reusable representation for organizing assumptions, variables, and relationships before analysis begins. As the final topic in this module, er-to-relational mapping carries the completed idea into relational model."}]}, {"id": "0e94117d-fe11-4aab-b90b-bb10b3618065", "type": "topic", "title": "Relational model", "description": "This module builds directly on conceptual modeling and develops relational model. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for sql foundations.", "children": [{"id": "c2574d0f-073b-40c5-b717-6f7942093877", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Keys", "children": [], "description": "Keys identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within relational model. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before integrity constraints because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "526a9b32-ee66-4f2c-b3f9-af0eb6aa0da5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Integrity constraints", "children": [], "description": "Integrity constraints is a governing quantity in relational model, linking local calculations to system-level behavior and offering a consistency check. After keys, integrity constraints supplies what is needed to address relational algebra."}, {"id": "f0bc7ef9-c14f-463b-85c0-9645b0670a7a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Relational algebra", "children": [], "description": "Relational algebra identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within relational model. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After integrity constraints, relational algebra supplies what is needed to address calculus intuition."}, {"id": "7534574b-b27f-4828-a1c0-986509de4f3d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Calculus intuition", "children": [], "description": "Calculus intuition identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within relational model. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, calculus intuition carries the completed idea into sql foundations."}]}, {"id": "347156c1-19d6-4a7c-b521-96b0c11301da", "type": "topic", "title": "SQL foundations", "description": "This module builds directly on relational model and develops sql foundations. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for schema design.", "children": [{"id": "7cbebb6e-aa17-4273-81c8-7897deadb5ce", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Selection", "children": [], "description": "Selection identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within sql foundations. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before joins because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "63c967b6-84c4-4c87-9459-cb3529885604", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Joins", "children": [], "description": "Joins identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within sql foundations. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After selection, joins supplies what is needed to address aggregation."}, {"id": "9bf4b976-974f-47f7-ad35-ecf88887fb5e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Aggregation", "children": [], "description": "Aggregation identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within sql foundations. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After joins, aggregation supplies what is needed to address subqueries."}, {"id": "e3adbe94-ed12-432f-b8d2-5b15b67bbb7b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Subqueries", "children": [], "description": "Subqueries identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within sql foundations. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After aggregation, subqueries supplies what is needed to address nulls."}, {"id": "6be56e5e-7851-44d5-9f29-be9b89189d6b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Nulls", "children": [], "description": "Nulls identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within sql foundations. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After subqueries, nulls supplies what is needed to address views."}, {"id": "483fff67-41e7-4164-b29a-48a2da60cc56", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Views", "children": [], "description": "Views identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within sql foundations. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, views carries the completed idea into schema design."}]}, {"id": "ca625efa-27af-4dd3-93a1-a57d17ae89c6", "type": "topic", "title": "Schema design", "description": "This module builds directly on sql foundations and develops schema design. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for storage.", "children": [{"id": "c0f50178-94df-4fe4-9f46-fe1f103e287d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Functional dependencies", "children": [], "description": "Functional dependencies identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within schema design. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before anomalies because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "6fe808d5-3245-48df-b779-9b0592ba5aab", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Anomalies", "children": [], "description": "Anomalies makes the validity limits of schema design explicit, showing when an otherwise correct method or system can become unreliable. After functional dependencies, anomalies supplies what is needed to address 3nf."}, {"id": "47507a3a-3fdd-40c4-9ca8-7fbe7d48ab97", "type": "subtopic", "title": "3NF", "children": [], "description": "3NF identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within schema design. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After anomalies, 3nf supplies what is needed to address bcnf."}, {"id": "08d9c202-5b40-4d01-8bcc-50ea3c452217", "type": "subtopic", "title": "BCNF", "children": [], "description": "BCNF identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within schema design. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After 3nf, bcnf supplies what is needed to address decomposition."}, {"id": "4df2ef12-f081-4920-a5bd-66fb52254645", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Decomposition", "children": [], "description": "Decomposition identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within schema design. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, decomposition carries the completed idea into storage."}]}, {"id": "8dce18d3-5145-4716-823c-946bc48209aa", "type": "topic", "title": "Storage", "description": "This module builds directly on schema design and develops storage. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for indexes.", "children": [{"id": "d34fc48b-6547-40a3-b271-5cd06687002f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Pages", "children": [], "description": "Pages identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within storage. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before records because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "9da37c93-8da4-4032-9329-f7cda366b80f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Records", "children": [], "description": "Records identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within storage. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After pages, records supplies what is needed to address buffer pools."}, {"id": "63ac564a-bc99-4ee6-9e7f-d0dbc8053fb9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Buffer pools", "children": [], "description": "Buffer pools identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within storage. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After records, buffer pools supplies what is needed to address file organizations."}, {"id": "6ea34a98-48ab-496c-9372-b44c5e7dde8f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "File organizations", "children": [], "description": "File organizations identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within storage. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After buffer pools, file organizations supplies what is needed to address cost models."}, {"id": "8ad002e4-4627-41d7-a893-217248fce14a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Cost models", "children": [], "description": "Cost models gives storage a reusable representation for organizing assumptions, variables, and relationships before analysis begins. As the final topic in this module, cost models carries the completed idea into indexes."}]}, {"id": "2bfe7559-c6fa-4d04-9c28-c8d0fc46662d", "type": "topic", "title": "Indexes", "description": "This module builds directly on storage and develops indexes. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for query processing.", "children": [{"id": "c9877a89-c4b5-420e-967c-23c2083bcce8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "B+ trees", "children": [], "description": "B+ trees identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within indexes. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before hashing because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "1e5edccf-72e2-4963-a6d7-697d50a0ff4d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Hashing", "children": [], "description": "Hashing identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within indexes. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After b+ trees, hashing supplies what is needed to address clustered vs unclustered."}, {"id": "1fb6d121-6cab-4a78-b8ee-d81b8247ecaf", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Clustered vs unclustered", "children": [], "description": "Clustered vs unclustered identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within indexes. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After hashing, clustered vs unclustered supplies what is needed to address composite indexes."}, {"id": "1cfa1f87-4c7d-4777-8563-f9e7b3627bdb", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Composite indexes", "children": [], "description": "Composite indexes is an executable part of indexes; its correctness, cost, and failure modes recur in later problems and implementations. As the final topic in this module, composite indexes carries the completed idea into query processing."}]}, {"id": "945c8530-6d10-4cef-bc74-0e10c2e8be40", "type": "topic", "title": "Query processing", "description": "This module builds directly on indexes and develops query processing. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for query optimization.", "children": [{"id": "c79421a2-e8a3-4a41-a032-6752839e9f73", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Scans", "children": [], "description": "Scans identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within query processing. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before external sort because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "69342940-0c61-41c3-8739-ad15d4b230e3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "External sort", "children": [], "description": "External sort identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within query processing. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After scans, external sort supplies what is needed to address join algorithms."}, {"id": "f2bc4adc-209f-40f2-8d1e-a4ded4941f3a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Join algorithms", "children": [], "description": "Join algorithms is an executable part of query processing; its correctness, cost, and failure modes recur in later problems and implementations. After external sort, join algorithms supplies what is needed to address pipelining."}, {"id": "bafb2360-6d5c-410c-9f2d-e3b3f8727936", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Pipelining", "children": [], "description": "Pipelining identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within query processing. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, pipelining carries the completed idea into query optimization."}]}, {"id": "9bdf8327-8ce7-4543-a9b0-ab6d42aa76e2", "type": "topic", "title": "Query optimization", "description": "This module builds directly on query processing and develops query optimization. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for transactions.", "children": [{"id": "e36f303d-6c75-426a-9ab1-edbdccd92f8f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Equivalences", "children": [], "description": "Equivalences identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within query optimization. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before cardinality estimation because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "2b32e7b0-c7e6-4a48-b449-b0e514edd449", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Cardinality estimation", "children": [], "description": "Cardinality estimation identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within query optimization. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After equivalences, cardinality estimation supplies what is needed to address access-path selection."}, {"id": "68e18edf-0252-4429-a9e8-219f47dbcb65", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Access-path selection", "children": [], "description": "Access-path selection identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within query optimization. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After cardinality estimation, access-path selection supplies what is needed to address plans."}, {"id": "4a336a4f-727f-4c10-bf3e-5f87a63dbb8f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Plans", "children": [], "description": "Plans identifies a specific object, distinction,