c43b6-a57e-4094-bedc-9b5617edf852", "type": "subtopic", "title": "MVCC concepts", "children": [], "description": "MVCC concepts identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within transactions. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, mvcc concepts carries the completed idea into recovery."}]}, {"id": "d99d7788-3698-4353-8885-29c4365d8ac8", "type": "topic", "title": "Recovery", "description": "This module builds directly on transactions and develops recovery. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for distributed and modern data systems.", "children": [{"id": "1d93bfc7-2bdb-4728-a82c-f945f5bdaa35", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Write-ahead logging", "children": [], "description": "Write-ahead logging identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within recovery. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before checkpoints because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "16f1f97c-dabc-4b7e-833b-f75fd56ddd4d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Checkpoints", "children": [], "description": "Checkpoints identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within recovery. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After write-ahead logging, checkpoints supplies what is needed to address undo/redo."}, {"id": "5e6925cc-509b-46ba-908c-d16c2e3bccc4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Undo/redo", "children": [], "description": "Undo/redo identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within recovery. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After checkpoints, undo/redo supplies what is needed to address crash scenarios."}, {"id": "1e5214a4-09d7-4851-905c-48bd399715df", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Crash scenarios", "children": [], "description": "Crash scenarios identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within recovery. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, crash scenarios carries the completed idea into distributed and modern data systems."}]}, {"id": "8300b62b-20a9-4197-abb8-1f3c3f613fe0", "type": "topic", "title": "Distributed and modern data systems", "description": "This culminating module draws on recovery and develops distributed and modern data systems. It belongs last because it requires the earlier tools to be selected, combined, and evaluated rather than used one at a time.", "children": [{"id": "531aa370-d7f7-469a-920e-b247e0753fc9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Partitioning", "children": [], "description": "Partitioning identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within distributed and modern data systems. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before replication because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "ec31daac-28d2-4a58-ba21-4b032d669aaa", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Replication", "children": [], "description": "Replication identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within distributed and modern data systems. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After partitioning, replication supplies what is needed to address cap tradeoffs."}, {"id": "41c2c5b7-7870-480d-bd87-6f0278263cf9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "CAP tradeoffs", "children": [], "description": "CAP tradeoffs identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within distributed and modern data systems. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After replication, cap tradeoffs supplies what is needed to address nosql fit."}, {"id": "bbf8d241-8792-482a-acf9-55903063036b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "NoSQL fit", "children": [], "description": "NoSQL fit identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within distributed and modern data systems. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final course topic, nosql fit requires ideas from the complete path to be integrated and transferred."}]}], "dbBacked": true}$dbsyszzjs$::jsonb,
